class:: MultiOUProcess
summary:: Correlated mean-reverting trajectories with temporal memory
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/OUProcess, Classes/MultiGaussNoise, Classes/LFNoise1

description::

MultiOUProcess creates several continuous stochastic trajectories that drift separately while sharing random innovations. Each component remembers its previous value and returns toward its mean; covariance relates its motion to the other components. Use it for ensemble breathing, coordinated spatial movement, and related parameter drift. link::Classes/MultiGaussNoise:: gives correlated values at trigger moments; MultiOUProcess gives correlated trajectories with memory through time.

It implements the diagonal-reversion multivariate Ornstein-Uhlenbeck SDE code::dX = -Theta*(X-mu)dt + B*dW::, where the buffer supplies diffusion covariance code::Sigma = B*B.transpose::. This extends the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process (Uhlenbeck and Ornstein, 1930), link::https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.36.823::. With code::s = theta_i+theta_j::, the exact innovation covariance is code::Q_ij = Sigma_ij * -expm1(-s*dt)/s::, or code::Sigma_ij*dt:: at s=0. Update is code::mu + exp(-theta*dt)*(X-mu) + L*z:: where code::L*L.transpose = Q::. Positive reversion gives stationary covariance code::Sigma_ij/(theta_i+theta_j)::, not Sigma itself.

Snapshots and Cholesky factorization happen at construction and explicit reload, never during ordinary updates. Covariance is symmetrized, then the same bounded jitter policy as MultiGaussNoise is used: eight attempts from code::max(largestDiagonal,1)*1e-12:: through 1e-5, followed by independent nonnegative diagonal variances. An exactly zero covariance remains zero. A missing/wrong-sized covariance uses identity diffusion; missing/wrong-sized optional vectors use zero means and unit reversions. Non-finite buffer entries become zero. All buffers must be mono; extra samples are ignored.

Reload preserves the current trajectory and RNG. Reset restores the loaded mean vector and seed, and suppresses a simultaneous reload. Constructor and reset start at the mean, so stationary variance builds over several reversion time constants. A non-finite or float-unrepresentable update restores the entire mean vector. Snapshot data are owned by the UGen; buffers are never modified. Sync buffer edits before sending a single reload edge. Large matrices make reload more expensive than ordinary O(N squared) updates.

Like link::Classes/LFNoise1:: it supports drifting modulation, but uses an exact stochastic transition with specified covariance and reversion rather than interpolated independent random targets.

